row.impact_if_wrong:
Darkrai is implemented correctly for every matchup in the table, so it does not explain the roughly 7-point underrating. Darkrai is a prime suspect in principle: 2 copies in the list, 20 per Darkrai at the end of every turn (both players') while the opponent's Active is Asleep, and Sing, Hypnoblast, Sleepy Lullaby and Dark Slumber make that common in most games. A bug here would push Altaria's win rate down. But every clause matches the card text and the recorded Pocket behaviour:
- timing before the Checkup;
- the ending player's effects first;
- works from the Bench and on turn 1;
- stacking;
- no Weakness and no attack reductions;
- Knock Out handling.

The one deviation I found would also lower Altaria's win rate: Bad Dreams wrongly blocked by "prevent damage by attacks" effects (Basic-only, all-damage and ≤X preventions). It needs a card that none of the 7 opponent lists contains, so it applies in 0% of the 28 matchups in the table. It only matters later if a list with such an attack joins the table.

Rule Darkrai out and look elsewhere for the Altaria gap.
